# Trivy ignore file, read by every Trivy scan in CI (image and config).
# Each entry must carry a written justification and a review date. An ignore
# without a reason is how a real finding gets buried.

# AWS-0104 - Security group rule allows unrestricted egress to any IP address.
#
# Applies to aws_security_group.backend and aws_security_group.frontend
# (egress cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]).
#
# Justification: both task types run in *private* subnets behind the ALB and
# reach the internet only through the NAT gateway. They must be able to call:
#   - the Gemini API (public internet, address range not enumerable)
#   - AWS control-plane endpoints (Secrets Manager, CloudWatch Logs, ECR, S3)
#     which do not all have gateway endpoints in every region
# Restricting egress to a static allow-list is not achievable for these
# destinations, and inbound is already constrained: the ALB security group is
# the only path in, and the database security group admits only the backend.
#
# Ingress is NOT ignored here and remains subject to the scan.
#
# Revisit if: VPC endpoints (secretsmanager / logs / ecr.api / s3) are added so
# that only Gemini needs public egress, at which point egress can be narrowed
# to 443/TCP and this entry should be deleted.
AWS-0104

# AWS-0054 - Listener for application load balancer does not use HTTPS.
#
# Justification: only the dev and staging defaults omit acm_certificate_arn
# and therefore create an HTTP listener. This is not left to the scanner to
# enforce - Terraform already refuses it. variables.tf declares
#
#   condition = var.environment != "production" || var.acm_certificate_arn != ""
#
# so `environment = "production"` cannot be planned or applied without a
# certificate, and the HTTP listener resource is not created at all when one
# is supplied. The scanner cannot tell dev from production in a single
# configuration, so suppressing it here is safe.
#
# Revisit if: the production path is ever made reachable without that
# validation - at which point this entry must be deleted, not merely
# re-documented.
AWS-0054
